    "annotated_text": "Nguyen, 2012: R1R2N H [reactant][STRUCTURE:R1R2NH] --(B(OH)3 [reagent][FORMULA:B(OH)3][NAME:boric acid][loading:10 mol%], H2O [reagent], DMF [ABBREVIATION][NAME:N,N-dimethylformamide][SMILES:CN(C)C=O], 150 °C; or HCONH2 [reagent][FORMULA:HCONH2][NAME:formamide], 25–150 °C)--> R1R2N(H)CHO [product][TRANSFORM:formylation / formamide formation]. Scope: primary amines [substrate], secondary amines [substrate], anilines [substrate], achiral substrates.\n\nSheppard, 2013: R1R2NH [reactant] --(B(OCH2CF3)3 [reagent][FORMULA:B(OCH2CF3)3][NAME:tris(2,2,2-trifluoroethoxy)borane][loading:2 equiv], DMF [ABBREVIATION][SMILES:CN(C)C=O]; MeCN [ABBREVIATION][NAME:acetonitrile][SMILES:CC#N], 5 h, 80 °C)--> R1R2N(H)CHO [product]. Scope: primary amines, 1 chiral substrate reported.\n\nThis study: R1R2NH [reactant] --(1 [reagent][IDENTIFIER:1][coref_bbox_id:3][SMILES:OB(c1ccccc1Cl)c1ccccc1Cl][NAME:boron-based precatalyst 1], 2.5–10 mol%; AcOH [reagent][ABBREVIATION][SMILES:CC(=O)O][loading:10–20 mol%]; DMF [ABBREVIATION][SMILES:CN(C)C=O], 25–85 °C or HCONH2 [reagent][SMILES:NC=O], 45 °C)--> R1R2N(H)CHO [product]. Scope: primary amines, secondary amines, α-aminoesters, chiral substrates.\n\nOverall reaction class: formylating transamidation (boron-catalyzed formylation of amines / transamidation) [reaction_type]. Scheme title: \"Formylating transamidations promoted by boron-based catalysts.\"",
